{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form supports synchronous, asynchronous, field-level, form-level, and\nStandard Schema validation. Every validator is an ordered object with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":"\nimplementation and explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggers"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"choose-when-validation-runs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose when validation runs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"change"},{"type":"text","value":" for immediate feedback and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"blur"},{"type":"text","value":" for feedback after leaving an\ninput. Submission runs validators by default regardless of their configured\nchange and blur triggers."}]},{"type":"code","value":"this.form.field(\n  {\n    name: 'age',\n    validators: [\n      {\n        triggers: ['change'],\n        run: ({ value }) =>\n          value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n      },\n      {\n        triggers: ['blur'],\n        run: ({ value }) => (value >= 0 ? undefined : 'Age cannot be negative'),\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  (field) => html`\n    <label>\n      Age\n      <input\n        name=${field.name}\n        type=\"number\"\n        .value=${String(field.value)}\n        @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n        @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n          field.handleChange(\n            (event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).valueAsNumber,\n          )}\n        aria-invalid=${field.meta.isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}\n      />\n      ${field.errors.map(\n        (error) => html`<span role=\"alert\">${error.message}</span>`,\n      )}\n    </label>\n  `,\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Additional controls include:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnMount"},{"type":"text","value":": run once when the form is constructed or when a field or form\ngroup first mounts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"runOnSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":": disable or conditionally enable submit-time execution."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"triggerDebounceMs"},{"type":"text","value":": debounce change and blur execution."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bailIfInvalid"},{"type":"text","value":": skip this and subsequent validators when an earlier one\nfailed."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"trigger objects with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"when"},{"type":"text","value":": enable a trigger conditionally."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"},{"type":"text","value":": rerun a field validator when related fields trigger it."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"control-when-errors-are-visible","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Control when errors are visible"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validation and presentation are separate. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" decides when field\nissues appear in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.errors"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"private form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  errorVisibility: ({ fieldState, state }) =>\n    fieldState.meta.isBlurred || state.submissionAttempts > 0,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta.original.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" for unfiltered issues when debugging or\nbuilding a custom visibility system."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"form-level-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form-level validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A form validator can produce a form issue and route issues to typed field paths\nwith "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createErrorMap"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"private form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: {\n    email: '',\n    phone: '',\n  },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n        const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n        if (!value.email && !value.phone) {\n          errors.form = 'Provide an email address or phone number'\n          errors.fields.email = 'Email is required when phone is empty'\n          errors.fields.phone = 'Phone is required when email is empty'\n        }\n\n        return errors\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.subscribe(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" to reactively select form-level issues from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.api.state.errors"},{"type":"text","value":". Lower-level integrations can subscribe to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.api.atom"},{"type":"text","value":".\nField-routed issues appear in the corresponding "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.errors"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"this.form.subscribe(\n  (state) => state.errors,\n  (errors) => html`\n    ${errors.map((error) => html`<p role=\"alert\">${error.message}</p>`)}\n  `,\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"asynchronous-validation-and-debouncing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Asynchronous validation and debouncing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":" may return a promise. Put cheap synchronous checks first and use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bailIfInvalid"},{"type":"text","value":" to avoid unnecessary requests:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"validators: [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'],\n    run: ({ value }) =>\n      value.length >= 3 ? undefined : 'Use at least 3 characters',\n  },\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'],\n    triggerDebounceMs: 500,\n    bailIfInvalid: true,\n    run: async ({ value }) => {\n      const available = await checkUsername(value)\n      return available ? undefined : 'That username is already taken'\n    },\n  },\n]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Submit validation always runs immediately, even when a trigger is debounced.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta.isValidating"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.api.state.isValidating"},{"type":"text","value":" expose pending work.\nRender form-wide pending state through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.subscribe(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" so it stays\nreactive."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"standard-schema-validation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Standard Schema validation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Any Standard Schema implementation can be supplied as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst accountSchema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  age: z.number().min(13),\n})\n\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: { email: '', age: 0 },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: accountSchema,\n    },\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Schema paths are routed to matching fields. Parsed outputs are available by\nvalidator index in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schemaOutputs"},{"type":"text","value":" during submit, for example\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schemaOutputs[0]"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" remains the raw editable state rather than the\nparsed output."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For custom schema routing, call a schema's safe-parse API inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"run"},{"type":"text","value":" and pass\nits issues to the provided "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"parseIssues"},{"type":"text","value":" helper."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"validate-related-fields","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Validate related fields"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"watchFields"},{"type":"text","value":" when one field's validity depends on another:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"this.form.field(\n  {\n    name: 'endDate',\n    validators: [\n      {\n        triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n        watchFields: ['startDate'],\n        run: ({ value, formApi }) =>\n          value >= formApi.getFieldValue('startDate')\n            ? undefined\n            : 'End date must be on or after the start date',\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  (field) => html`\n    <input\n      name=${field.name}\n      type=\"date\"\n      .value=${field.value}\n      @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n      @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n        field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).value)}\n      aria-invalid=${field.meta.isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}\n    />\n  `,\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"return-errors-from-submission","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return errors from submission"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Endpoint validation belongs in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":". Return\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createValidationError(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" to feed server issues back into normal form state:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"private form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value, createValidationError }) => {\n    const result = await saveProfile(value)\n\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      return createValidationError({\n        form: 'Could not save the profile',\n        fields: { email: 'This email is already registered' },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return null\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"prevent-invalid-submission","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prevent invalid submission"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.api.handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" skips "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" when validation fails and resolves\nwith the validation errors. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSubmitInvalid"},{"type":"text","value":" is currently available on form\ngroups; root-form support is planned but not yet implemented. Subscribe to\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canSubmit"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isSubmitting"},{"type":"text","value":" to reflect that state in the submit UI:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"this.form.subscribe(\n  (state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting] as const,\n  ([canSubmit, isSubmitting]) => html`\n    <button type=\"submit\" ?disabled=${!canSubmit || isSubmitting}>\n      ${isSubmitting ? 'Submitting…' : 'Submit'}\n    </button>\n  `,\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a disabled submit button would hide useful validation feedback, keep it\nfocusable with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aria-disabled"},{"type":"text","value":" and let "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleSubmit()"},{"type":"text","value":" report the issues."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"choose-when-validation-runs","text":"Choose when validation runs","level":2},{"id":"control-when-errors-are-visible","text":"Control when errors are visible","level":2},{"id":"form-level-validation","text":"Form-level validation","level":2},{"id":"asynchronous-validation-and-debouncing","text":"Asynchronous validation and debouncing","level":2},{"id":"standard-schema-validation","text":"Standard Schema validation","level":2},{"id":"validate-related-fields","text":"Validate related fields","level":2},{"id":"return-errors-from-submission","text":"Return errors from submission","level":2},{"id":"prevent-invalid-submission","text":"Prevent invalid submission","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Form supports synchronous, asynchronous, field-level, form-level, and\nStandard Schema validation. Every validator is an ordered object with a `run`\nimplementation and explicit `triggers`.\n\n## Choose when validation runs\n\nUse `change` for immediate feedback and `blur` for feedback after leaving an\ninput. Submission runs validators by default regardless of their configured\nchange and blur triggers.\n\n```ts\nthis.form.field(\n  {\n    name: 'age',\n    validators: [\n      {\n        triggers: ['change'],\n        run: ({ value }) =>\n          value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n      },\n      {\n        triggers: ['blur'],\n        run: ({ value }) => (value >= 0 ? undefined : 'Age cannot be negative'),\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  (field) => html`\n    <label>\n      Age\n      <input\n        name=${field.name}\n        type=\"number\"\n        .value=${String(field.value)}\n        @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n        @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n          field.handleChange(\n            (event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).valueAsNumber,\n          )}\n        aria-invalid=${field.meta.isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}\n      />\n      ${field.errors.map(\n        (error) => html`<span role=\"alert\">${error.message}</span>`,\n      )}\n    </label>\n  `,\n)\n```\n\nAdditional controls include:\n\n- `runOnMount`: run once when the form is constructed or when a field or form\n  group first mounts.\n- `runOnSubmit`: disable or conditionally enable submit-time execution.\n- `triggerDebounceMs`: debounce change and blur execution.\n- `bailIfInvalid`: skip this and subsequent validators when an earlier one\n  failed.\n- trigger objects with `when`: enable a trigger conditionally.\n- `watchFields`: rerun a field validator when related fields trigger it.\n\n## Control when errors are visible\n\nValidation and presentation are separate. `errorVisibility` decides when field\nissues appear in `field.errors`:\n\n```ts\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  errorVisibility: ({ fieldState, state }) =>\n    fieldState.meta.isBlurred || state.submissionAttempts > 0,\n})\n```\n\nUse `field.meta.original.errors` for unfiltered issues when debugging or\nbuilding a custom visibility system.\n\n## Form-level validation\n\nA form validator can produce a form issue and route issues to typed field paths\nwith `createErrorMap`:\n\n```ts\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: {\n    email: '',\n    phone: '',\n  },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n        const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n        if (!value.email && !value.phone) {\n          errors.form = 'Provide an email address or phone number'\n          errors.fields.email = 'Email is required when phone is empty'\n          errors.fields.phone = 'Phone is required when email is empty'\n        }\n\n        return errors\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nUse `form.subscribe(...)` to reactively select form-level issues from\n`form.api.state.errors`. Lower-level integrations can subscribe to\n`form.api.atom`.\nField-routed issues appear in the corresponding `field.errors`.\n\n```ts\nthis.form.subscribe(\n  (state) => state.errors,\n  (errors) => html`\n    ${errors.map((error) => html`<p role=\"alert\">${error.message}</p>`)}\n  `,\n)\n```\n\n## Asynchronous validation and debouncing\n\n`run` may return a promise. Put cheap synchronous checks first and use\n`bailIfInvalid` to avoid unnecessary requests:\n\n```ts\nvalidators: [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'],\n    run: ({ value }) =>\n      value.length >= 3 ? undefined : 'Use at least 3 characters',\n  },\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'],\n    triggerDebounceMs: 500,\n    bailIfInvalid: true,\n    run: async ({ value }) => {\n      const available = await checkUsername(value)\n      return available ? undefined : 'That username is already taken'\n    },\n  },\n]\n```\n\nSubmit validation always runs immediately, even when a trigger is debounced.\n`field.meta.isValidating` and `form.api.state.isValidating` expose pending work.\nRender form-wide pending state through `form.subscribe(...)` so it stays\nreactive.\n\n## Standard Schema validation\n\nAny Standard Schema implementation can be supplied as `run`:\n\n```ts\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst accountSchema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  age: z.number().min(13),\n})\n\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: { email: '', age: 0 },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: accountSchema,\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nSchema paths are routed to matching fields. Parsed outputs are available by\nvalidator index in `schemaOutputs` during submit, for example\n`schemaOutputs[0]`. `value` remains the raw editable state rather than the\nparsed output.\n\nFor custom schema routing, call a schema's safe-parse API inside `run` and pass\nits issues to the provided `parseIssues` helper.\n\n## Validate related fields\n\nUse `watchFields` when one field's validity depends on another:\n\n```ts\nthis.form.field(\n  {\n    name: 'endDate',\n    validators: [\n      {\n        triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n        watchFields: ['startDate'],\n        run: ({ value, formApi }) =>\n          value >= formApi.getFieldValue('startDate')\n            ? undefined\n            : 'End date must be on or after the start date',\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  (field) => html`\n    <input\n      name=${field.name}\n      type=\"date\"\n      .value=${field.value}\n      @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n      @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n        field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).value)}\n      aria-invalid=${field.meta.isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}\n    />\n  `,\n)\n```\n\n## Return errors from submission\n\nEndpoint validation belongs in `onSubmit`. Return\n`createValidationError(...)` to feed server issues back into normal form state:\n\n```ts\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value, createValidationError }) => {\n    const result = await saveProfile(value)\n\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      return createValidationError({\n        form: 'Could not save the profile',\n        fields: { email: 'This email is already registered' },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return null\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Prevent invalid submission\n\n`form.api.handleSubmit()` skips `onSubmit` when validation fails and resolves\nwith the validation errors. `onSubmitInvalid` is currently available on form\ngroups; root-form support is planned but not yet implemented. Subscribe to\n`canSubmit` and `isSubmitting` to reflect that state in the submit UI:\n\n```ts\nthis.form.subscribe(\n  (state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting] as const,\n  ([canSubmit, isSubmitting]) => html`\n    <button type=\"submit\" ?disabled=${!canSubmit || isSubmitting}>\n      ${isSubmitting ? 'Submitting…' : 'Submit'}\n    </button>\n  `,\n)\n```\n\nIf a disabled submit button would hide useful validation feedback, keep it\nfocusable with `aria-disabled` and let `handleSubmit()` report the issues.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: form-validation\ntitle: Form and Field Validation\n---\n\nTanStack Form supports synchronous, asynchronous, field-level, form-level, and\nStandard Schema validation. Every validator is an ordered object with a `run`\nimplementation and explicit `triggers`.\n\n## Choose when validation runs\n\nUse `change` for immediate feedback and `blur` for feedback after leaving an\ninput. Submission runs validators by default regardless of their configured\nchange and blur triggers.\n\n```ts\nthis.form.field(\n  {\n    name: 'age',\n    validators: [\n      {\n        triggers: ['change'],\n        run: ({ value }) =>\n          value >= 13 ? undefined : 'You must be at least 13',\n      },\n      {\n        triggers: ['blur'],\n        run: ({ value }) => (value >= 0 ? undefined : 'Age cannot be negative'),\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  (field) => html`\n    <label>\n      Age\n      <input\n        name=${field.name}\n        type=\"number\"\n        .value=${String(field.value)}\n        @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n        @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n          field.handleChange(\n            (event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).valueAsNumber,\n          )}\n        aria-invalid=${field.meta.isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}\n      />\n      ${field.errors.map(\n        (error) => html`<span role=\"alert\">${error.message}</span>`,\n      )}\n    </label>\n  `,\n)\n```\n\nAdditional controls include:\n\n- `runOnMount`: run once when the form is constructed or when a field or form\n  group first mounts.\n- `runOnSubmit`: disable or conditionally enable submit-time execution.\n- `triggerDebounceMs`: debounce change and blur execution.\n- `bailIfInvalid`: skip this and subsequent validators when an earlier one\n  failed.\n- trigger objects with `when`: enable a trigger conditionally.\n- `watchFields`: rerun a field validator when related fields trigger it.\n\n## Control when errors are visible\n\nValidation and presentation are separate. `errorVisibility` decides when field\nissues appear in `field.errors`:\n\n```ts\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  errorVisibility: ({ fieldState, state }) =>\n    fieldState.meta.isBlurred || state.submissionAttempts > 0,\n})\n```\n\nUse `field.meta.original.errors` for unfiltered issues when debugging or\nbuilding a custom visibility system.\n\n## Form-level validation\n\nA form validator can produce a form issue and route issues to typed field paths\nwith `createErrorMap`:\n\n```ts\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: {\n    email: '',\n    phone: '',\n  },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value, createErrorMap }) => {\n        const errors = createErrorMap()\n\n        if (!value.email && !value.phone) {\n          errors.form = 'Provide an email address or phone number'\n          errors.fields.email = 'Email is required when phone is empty'\n          errors.fields.phone = 'Phone is required when email is empty'\n        }\n\n        return errors\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nUse `form.subscribe(...)` to reactively select form-level issues from\n`form.api.state.errors`. Lower-level integrations can subscribe to\n`form.api.atom`.\nField-routed issues appear in the corresponding `field.errors`.\n\n```ts\nthis.form.subscribe(\n  (state) => state.errors,\n  (errors) => html`\n    ${errors.map((error) => html`<p role=\"alert\">${error.message}</p>`)}\n  `,\n)\n```\n\n## Asynchronous validation and debouncing\n\n`run` may return a promise. Put cheap synchronous checks first and use\n`bailIfInvalid` to avoid unnecessary requests:\n\n```ts\nvalidators: [\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'],\n    run: ({ value }) =>\n      value.length >= 3 ? undefined : 'Use at least 3 characters',\n  },\n  {\n    triggers: ['change'],\n    triggerDebounceMs: 500,\n    bailIfInvalid: true,\n    run: async ({ value }) => {\n      const available = await checkUsername(value)\n      return available ? undefined : 'That username is already taken'\n    },\n  },\n]\n```\n\nSubmit validation always runs immediately, even when a trigger is debounced.\n`field.meta.isValidating` and `form.api.state.isValidating` expose pending work.\nRender form-wide pending state through `form.subscribe(...)` so it stays\nreactive.\n\n## Standard Schema validation\n\nAny Standard Schema implementation can be supplied as `run`:\n\n```ts\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst accountSchema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  age: z.number().min(13),\n})\n\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: { email: '', age: 0 },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: accountSchema,\n    },\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nSchema paths are routed to matching fields. Parsed outputs are available by\nvalidator index in `schemaOutputs` during submit, for example\n`schemaOutputs[0]`. `value` remains the raw editable state rather than the\nparsed output.\n\nFor custom schema routing, call a schema's safe-parse API inside `run` and pass\nits issues to the provided `parseIssues` helper.\n\n## Validate related fields\n\nUse `watchFields` when one field's validity depends on another:\n\n```ts\nthis.form.field(\n  {\n    name: 'endDate',\n    validators: [\n      {\n        triggers: ['change', 'blur'],\n        watchFields: ['startDate'],\n        run: ({ value, formApi }) =>\n          value >= formApi.getFieldValue('startDate')\n            ? undefined\n            : 'End date must be on or after the start date',\n      },\n    ],\n  },\n  (field) => html`\n    <input\n      name=${field.name}\n      type=\"date\"\n      .value=${field.value}\n      @blur=${() => field.handleBlur()}\n      @input=${(event: InputEvent) =>\n        field.handleChange((event.currentTarget as HTMLInputElement).value)}\n      aria-invalid=${field.meta.isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}\n    />\n  `,\n)\n```\n\n## Return errors from submission\n\nEndpoint validation belongs in `onSubmit`. Return\n`createValidationError(...)` to feed server issues back into normal form state:\n\n```ts\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: { email: '' },\n  onSubmit: async ({ value, createValidationError }) => {\n    const result = await saveProfile(value)\n\n    if (!result.ok) {\n      return createValidationError({\n        form: 'Could not save the profile',\n        fields: { email: 'This email is already registered' },\n      })\n    }\n\n    return null\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Prevent invalid submission\n\n`form.api.handleSubmit()` skips `onSubmit` when validation fails and resolves\nwith the validation errors. `onSubmitInvalid` is currently available on form\ngroups; root-form support is planned but not yet implemented. Subscribe to\n`canSubmit` and `isSubmitting` to reflect that state in the submit UI:\n\n```ts\nthis.form.subscribe(\n  (state) => [state.canSubmit, state.isSubmitting] as const,\n  ([canSubmit, isSubmitting]) => html`\n    <button type=\"submit\" ?disabled=${!canSubmit || isSubmitting}>\n      ${isSubmitting ? 'Submitting…' : 'Submit'}\n    </button>\n  `,\n)\n```\n\nIf a disabled submit button would hide useful validation feedback, keep it\nfocusable with `aria-disabled` and let `handleSubmit()` report the issues.\n"}
